WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.028
Hi, friends. This is In Their Shoes.

00:00:13.028 --> 00:00:18.055
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:18.055 --> 00:00:21.072
Hands flat on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:21.072 --> 00:00:24.088
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:24.088 --> 00:00:32.133
Every person has moments — happy ones, hard ones, and everything in between.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:42.188
When we step into their shoes, we imagine their moment from the inside. The shoes are pretend — the imagining is real.

00:00:42.188 --> 00:00:49.227
We cannot know exactly what someone feels. But imagining helps us choose kindness.

00:00:49.227 --> 00:00:55.260
Let's practice. Picture a classmate on their very first day of school.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:02.298
It is lunchtime. They stand with their tray, looking for a place to sit.

00:01:02.298 --> 00:01:10.343
Now step into their shoes. You are holding the tray, looking at all the tables.

00:01:10.343 --> 00:01:17.381
What might they feel? Maybe nervous. Maybe lonely. Maybe a little of both.

00:01:17.381 --> 00:01:23.414
Name it quietly to yourself: "They might feel lonely." Naming it helps you understand.

00:01:23.414 --> 00:01:29.448
Now choose a kind thing: make a space, smile, and say, "You can sit here."

00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:38.497
One more pair of shoes. Picture a classmate whose tall block tower fell down right at the end.

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:44.530
Step into their shoes. You worked so hard on it… and down it went.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:52.575
What might they feel? Maybe disappointed. Maybe frustrated. Name it quietly: "That would feel disappointing."

00:01:52.575 --> 00:01:58.608
Choose a kind thing: "That tower looked great. Want help building it again?"

00:01:58.608 --> 00:02:06.652
You imagined. You named the feeling. You chose kindness. That is In Their Shoes.

00:02:06.652 --> 00:02:15.702
You won't always know what someone feels. That is okay. Noticing, and being gentle, is the kind part.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:18.718
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:18.718 --> 00:02:22.740
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.762
You're ready for what's next.
